course: dictionary
lesson: 4282
title: Greek: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Greek can mean a country, a person, a language, or a phrase. Context tells you which meaning is right. «The Greeks invented theatre, with comedies and tragedies performed in great open-air theatres.» Here Greeks means people, because people invent things.
explain: Ask what job the word does in the sentence. Is it a thing, or is it describing something? «Greek myths» describes the stories, so Greek means from Greece. «Greek is the language spoken in Greece» is about the language. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Some Greek words are used in set phrases, which you learn as a whole. «It's all Greek to me» does not mean anything about Greece. It means «I can't understand it at all». When a phrase sounds strange, read the whole sentence and think about what the speaker is trying to say.
fact: Greek means from or about Greece, a country in southern Europe.
fact: A Greek is a person from Greece, and the plural is Greeks.
fact: Greek is also a language, with its own alphabet: alpha, beta, gamma and so on.
fact: «It's all Greek to me» means «I can't understand it at all».
fact: Many English words come from Greek, such as telephone and geography.
exercise: «The Greeks invented theatre, with comedies and tragedies performed in great open-air theatres.» In this sentence, what does Greeks mean? | A kind of theatre mask | *People from Greece long ago | A small boat | A language spoken in Greece
exercise: Sam says, «It's all Greek to me.» What does Sam mean? | I like Greek food | I speak Greek very well | I am going to Greece next week | *I can't understand it at all
exercise: Which Greek letter, written as π, is used in maths? | Gamma | Alpha | *Pi
test: «Greeks sailed in triremes, fast warships with three rows of oars, and traded olive oil, wine and pottery.» What is a trireme? | A Greek letter | A kind of olive | *A fast warship with three rows of oars | A water clock
test: Which word in English comes from Greek? | *Telephone | Window | Running | Happy
exam: Which sentence uses Greek to mean the language? | *«Octopus comes from Greek» | «Greeks sailed in triremes» | «The Greeks invented theatre» | «It's all Greek to me»
